Patch 0081: the common case of dispatchGuestBranch is inline.
What: PS2Runtime::dispatchGuestBranch (every inter-function transfer of the recompiled code) was an out-of-line call; its
common case (the EE checkpoint says "not due", the transfer is a call, and the target is in the function table) is now an
inline function (runtime/ps2_dispatch_inline.h, included at the end of ee_scheduler.h). Everything else is in
dispatchGuestBranchTail(), which holds the old body after the checkpoint. The 8-cycle charge, the checkpoint point and the
dispatch history (DON_DISPATCH_HISTORY, now a plain bool read per call) behave as before.
Verified: perf_fight.py (4-player fight, blanks 6000-7800): state hash a71d52ac6fe9b90e639d4e7d33808bbd6ecd50e0d1c28f1c8e67fac6b07906e5,
equal to the reference, with this patch in the binary; the linux-dev build passes.
Original work, GPL-3.0.
